-- Issue-stage events, relative to the middle's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.middle).
--
-- These are the events the retire counters cannot answer: the counters say how many, these say when and in what order.
-- The two stage registers are the middle's, so the issue events share its scope with the retire file; bind both, e.g.
-- for the redirect each issue turns into (the window is the read/write-back distance, so it is not a fixed number):
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/src/middle/issue.pulse <MIDDLE> Middle \
--       --event nzea_core/src/middle/retire.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Middle.uop_issue ->1 Core.redirect'

-- There is an instruction in the issue stage: the uop the units work on, or a payload waiting for its operands.
inflight = isexValid || idisValid

-- A uop's first cycle in the execute slot: the cycle after the read placed its operands, and the one the units take as
-- the uop's beginning.
uop_issue = slotFirst

-- The payload holds although the execute slot is free: what stops it is its own operands — it reads the very
-- instruction that is finishing below it, and the write it waits for lands a cycle later. `decoded_ready` is the
-- register's accept side; while `idisValid` holds and no flush is up it is the read's own ready, which is where the
-- operand check lives.
operand_wait = idisValid && !decoded_ready && (!isexValid || complete_valid) && !flushing
